## Milestone Design Rationale

**Why max_distance=5 for all find tasks:**
- All targets are 11-19 blocks from spawn
- With max_distance=5, the player must navigate to within 5 blocks of target
- This means minimum 6-14 blocks of travel from spawn before any find milestone triggers
- Combined with facing_tolerance=60°, this prevents accidental/trivial completion

**Why facing_tolerance=60 uniformly:**
- 60° cone is generous enough to allow natural looking behavior
- Tight enough to confirm intentional observation (not just passing by while looking elsewhere)
- Works well for both eye-level targets (banners, pots) and ground-level targets (slabs, tulips, terracotta)

**Gray terracotta target adjustment:**
- Moved target from y=-1 (the block itself) to y=0 (air above the floor)
- This means the player standing in the room and looking generally at the floor area will satisfy the check
- Avoids requiring an unnaturally steep downward gaze

**Dependency enforcement through spatial separation:**
- South wing targets (tulip → coral → mushroom) are progressively further from spawn: 11.4 → 14.1 → 19.2 blocks
- North wing targets (banner/slab → terracotta → concrete) are progressively deeper: 12.0 → 15.0 → 16.4 blocks
- The milestone evaluation order ensures earlier milestones must be checked before later ones

